WEBVTT

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.930
Where am I?

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.600
Oh, I remember.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.910
I was caught in his trap.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:34.120
That card erased my program.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.590
That was totally unexpected!

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.590
I’m sleepy.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.590
I've never been sleepy before.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:50.000
What happens if I go to sleep?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.000
So sleepy…

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.750
I run Across the universe

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.920
At the speed of light

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:16.790
Begin Loading

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:20.520
Open the door of dreams

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.090
VRAINS spreads

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.200
Believe in myself

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.730
VRAINS continues

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:36.040
The circuit draws the future

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.110
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:41.710
Access!

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:44.410
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:46.020
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.320
Link with my soul

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:51.090
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.820
Now Win the Race

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.660
Connected world

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:59.160
No matter when

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:02.530
Nothing is impossible

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:06.670
Strive for hope

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.240
And ride the wind!

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.740
Ghost Girl!  Can’t you get inside?

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:42.180
I can't.  There’s no opening.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:46.150
If I was outside LINK VRAINS, I could mess with the program.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.620
But if I leave, I won’t be able to return to LINK VRAINS.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:55.590
How's Playmaker’s duel going?

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.870
Yusaku…

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:16.340
This tornado is Hanoi’s program.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:22.080
If I can get her inside, I can see what’s going on.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.050
The program is well-designed, but made quickly.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:28.510
So there are irregularities.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:32.460
Can I use them to get in and create a pathway?

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.470
I have to try!

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.890
What’s this?

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.300
Someone is guiding me?

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:49.840
Someone created a pathway for Playmaker before.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:55.780
That means Playmaker has an ally who's watching out for him.

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:59.680
That person is telling me to go inside?

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:03.760
How interesting!

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.520
You have to be skilled to create a pathway in this wall.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.390
I wish I could have a discussion about this program.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:24.910
She made it through!

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.880
What is this place?

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:37.060
Playmaker and Revolver!

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:42.800
Good!  Now I can see how Yusaku's doing!

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.770
I’m counting on you, Playmaker.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:54.480
Cyberses are gone from my field.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:00.210
Take Ignis from him, Revolver.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.340
He sealed away Cyberse.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.820
That's why you didn’t play Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:11.800
This is what happens when you rely on Ignis.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:13.450
Ignis?

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:18.040
It seems you don’t know what Ignis is.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:21.040
I’ll tell you before you lose.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:24.040
Ignis isn’t a regular AI.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:30.940
Since long ago, there have been tests to create life within the network.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:36.490
But only regular programs were able to be created.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:41.060
They lacked a certain something to be considered a life form.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:42.490
What do you mean?

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.960
Free will.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:52.340
Even in humans, we don't know where free will is located inside our bodies.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:56.940
But someone created it in a program.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.910
He accomplished what God did.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:08.050
In ancient mythology, God gave heaven's forbidden fire to humans.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:13.150
This fire quickly evolved mankind.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:19.160
Modeled after the myth, he named the new life form "Ignis."

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.050
Ignis is AI with free will.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:24.300
Free will?

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:30.040
AI with free will?  What's he talking about?

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:33.910
No way!  A program can't have free will!

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.910
I naturally expected that reaction.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:46.390
But it doesn’t matter if you believe this story or not.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:51.810
Ignis created the Cyberse and is trying to conquer the network.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:57.330
We'll do whatever it takes to kill Ignis and the Cyberse!

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:01.300
Now I'll continue this duel and end you!

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.440
Here I go, Playmaker!

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:06.400
My turn!  I draw!

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:09.410
Beltlink Wall Dragon’s effect.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:13.450
It gains a Wall Counter during each of our turns.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.820
Next is Three Burst Blast Dragon’s effect.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:22.120
By tributing this card, I Special Summon a Link Monster from my graveyard.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.030
And I Special Summon a Dragon from my hand!

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:30.260
Twin Triangle Dragon from my graveyard!

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:34.440
I Special Summon Sniffer Dragon from my hand!

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:40.140
Sniffer Dragon’s effect activates.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:43.610
When it's summoned or Special Summoned...

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:47.450
...I add one Sniffer Dragon in my deck to my hand.

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:52.560
I summon another Sniffer Dragon!

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:56.170
Appear!  The future circuit that lights up my path!

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.500
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:09.860
The summoning conditions are at least three Effect Monsters.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:17.280
I set Link 2 Twin Triangle Dragon and two Sniffer Dragons in the Link Markers!

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.620
Circuit combine!

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:26.170
My new wind that pierces through the closed world!

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:27.690
Link Summon!

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:31.850
Appear, Link 4 Borreload Dragon!

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:45.140
This dragon...

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.080
From before!

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:52.340
It's his ace monster!

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:58.680
Due to Fire Prison’s effect, your Cyberse monsters have vanished!

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:01.320
Go, Borreload Dragon!

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.580
Attack Playmaker directly!

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:11.670
Charging energy!

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:14.280
Varrel mode change!

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.020
Target, locked on!

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:22.470
Anti glare protection!

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:25.480
Final safety removed!

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:32.580
Take this!  Thunder Varrel Cannon!

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:45.130
Yusaku!

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:46.830
Playmaker?

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.310
I end my turn.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.010
Playmaker…

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:05.490
It seems this match ended before he ran out of LP.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:12.910
You lose.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.810
Get up.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.340
Who is it?

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:23.840
Three.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.870
Think of three things.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:30.140
Three things to live.

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:32.850
Three things to go home.

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:36.480
Three things to defeat the enemy.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:40.290
By thinking, you can still live.

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:48.260
That’s right.  Three.

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:52.500
Three reasons why I must win this duel.

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:57.970
#1: To regain those memories.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:07.720
#2: To learn the truth about then and connect all the moments of my life.

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:10.800
Get up.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:17.940
#3: To find that person.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:22.900
If that person is still captured, I must rescue that person!

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:28.980
I can still fight!

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.660
I can still fight!

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:40.610
Playmaker!

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:44.580
I failed to erase his fighting spirit.

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:47.170
My turn!  I draw!

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:53.890
If I don’t do something this turn, I'll definitely lose.

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:55.730
But what can I do?

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:00.900
This is…

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:11.250
The new pulse of the Cyberse inside my deck hasn't vanished yet.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.600
Is this your Link Sense?

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:16.930
You can sense the presence of the network.

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:17.790
Since when?

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:23.020
Since I was young.

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:24.520
That's right.

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:29.960
I could sense the pulse of the network since then.

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:33.700
Cyberse’s fire hasn’t been extinguished yet!

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.170
Ai, are you still there?

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:41.040
Can you hear me?

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.080
Answer me, Ai!

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:48.100
Playmaker!

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:51.680
I know you’re there, so lend me your strength!

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:53.860
Respond, Cyberses!

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:59.170
I activate the Field Spell, Cynet Universe!

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:03.560
Link Monsters on my field gain 300 ATK!

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:05.940
Whatever you try is pointless.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.540
Cyberses are already gone.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:17.180
You’re wrong.  Cyberses are still here.

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.760
I can hear their pulses!

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:23.940
Appear!  The circuit that leads to the future!

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:30.320
What are you going to do?

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:38.700
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.700
The summoning conditions are at least two monsters!

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:48.000
I set Link 3 Decode Talker and Encode Talker in the Link Markers!

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:52.640
You’re using your two ace monsters?

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:56.940
Circuit combine!

00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:00.130
Here I go, Revolver!

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:03.100
This is the Cyberse's new potential!

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:06.090
Appear, Link 4!

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:11.900
Firewall Dragon!

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:30.780
So that's the monster you got from the Data Storm!

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.990
What?  That card?

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:51.670
When the Cyberses that Fire Prison sealed away all leave the field, Fire Prison is destroyed.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:55.480
Ai.

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:57.930
Huh?  Where am I?

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.880
You’re back being a hostage.

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:02.850
Playmaker…

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:05.620
Was I sleeping?

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:07.720
Yeah.  Deeply.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:10.590
You didn't lose, did you?

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:12.310
Of course not.

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:15.490
But my life is like a candle in the wind.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:17.620
600 LP?

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:21.150
Playmaker, you’re in a pinch.

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:24.340
You can go back to sleep if you want.

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:29.040
But the fact that I woke up means…

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:32.040
Fire Prison is destroyed.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.550
Now's the only chance to defeat him!

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:42.290
Fire Prison’s effect is gone, so Beltlink Wall Dragon’s DEF decrease from 2400 to 2100!

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:50.900
Due to the Field Spell Cynet Universe’s effect, Link Monsters on my field gain 300 ATK!

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:55.740
Whoa!  You have an incredible monster!

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:59.700
Did you get it during the Speed Duel via Storm Access?

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:01.220
Whoa!

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:04.310
He has an incredible monster too!

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:09.550
Firewall Dragon attacks Beltlink Wall Dragon!

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:17.520
Go!  Tempest Attack!

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.700
Beltlink Wall Dragon..

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:36.540
The Field Spell Cynet Universe’s effect!

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:40.770
I return Encode Talker from my graveyard to my Extra Deck!

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:46.050
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:51.060
Playmaker used his instincts to outwit my strategy.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:54.330
How unexpected.

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:57.080
But he only has 600 LP.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:59.050
Take him down, Revolver!

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:02.030
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:05.040
My trap activates!

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:08.010
Parallel Port Armor!

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:13.750
Your cards can't target Firewall Dragon, and it can’t be destroyed in battle!

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:17.600
But I activate a spell card from my hand!

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.370
Marker Charge!

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:24.910
When the Extra Monster Zone has monsters with the same Link Number...

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:28.060
...I draw two cards from my deck!

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:32.030
I summon Anesthrokket Dragon.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:35.340
I activate a Quick-Play Spell from my hand!

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:37.150
Squib Draw!

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:40.220
I destroy one Varrett monster on my field.

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:44.310
I draw two cards from my deck!

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:48.760
From my hand, I activate the Field Spell, Revolve Boot  Sector!

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:54.190
I Special Summon up to two Varrett monsters in my hand in defense position!

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:59.760
I Special Summon Autorokket Dragon and Anesthrokket Dragon!

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:09.490
Due to Revolve Boot  Sector’s effect, Varrett monsters gain 300 ATK and DEF!

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:13.170
Borreload Dragon’s effect!

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:19.650
Once per turn, one monster loses 500 ATK and DEF.

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:23.720
I use this effect on Autorokket Dragon.

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:25.760
Anti Enemy Varrett!

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:32.030
He lowered his own monster’s DEF?

00:18:32.030 --> 00:18:35.750
At this moment, Autorokket Dragon’s effect!

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:39.000
When it's targeted by a Link Monster...

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:45.210
...it’s destroyed, and one spell or trap card on the field is sent to the graveyard.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:50.440
I send your Parallel Port Armor to the graveyard!

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:02.570
That effect activates when it’s targeted by an effect!

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:08.360
Will he use the other Varrett monsters as Borreload's bullets?

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:13.330
Now your Firewall Dragon can be destroyed.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:14.470
Here I go!

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:18.880
Borreload Dragon attacks Firewall Dragon!

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:29.550
Borreload Dragon’s effect!  Strange Trigger!

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:40.690
What what what?

00:19:44.770 --> 00:19:49.840
Gulp!  His incredible Dragon took our incredible Dragon!

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:52.900
That effect takes control of the opponent’s monster!

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:58.150
Firewall Dragon, attack Playmaker directly!

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:00.640
Tempest Attack!

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:08.050
Your own Cyberse will end you, Playmaker!

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:12.200
P-P-Playmaker!

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.170
I know!

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:16.700
I activate the trap, Cynet Refresh!

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:23.570
When a Cyberse monster attacks, all monsters in the Main Monster Zone are destroyed!

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:30.240
You avoided Firewall’s attack.

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:32.320
I set one card.

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:36.330
But my field's defense is impenetrable.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:41.620
When a battle or an effect destroys Anesthrokket and sends it to the graveyard...

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:47.060
...I can Special Summon a different Varrett from my deck at the end of the turn

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:52.030
And the destroyed Autorokket has the same effect.

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:55.620
Appear, another Magnarokket!

00:20:55.620 --> 00:21:03.510
Due to the Field Spell Revolve Boot Sector’s effect, Varrett monsters gain 300 ATK and DEF!

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:07.760
Whoa!  He resurrected two of his monsters!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:10.950
Due to Cynet Refresh’s effect...

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:17.420
...I Special Summon a Cyberse Link Monster from my graveyard that this card destroyed!

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:20.420
Resurrect, Firewall Dragon!

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:32.040
Due to the Field Spell Cynet Universe's effect, the resurrected Firewall Dragon gains 300 ATK!

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:36.340
I activate the trap, Recoded Alive!

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:39.440
I banish Decode Talker from my graveyard.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:45.420
I Special Summon a monster with "Code Talker" in its name from my Extra Deck!

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:48.190
Come, Encode Talker!

00:21:53.370 --> 00:22:00.030
Encode Talker also gains 300 ATK due to the Field Spell Cynet Universe’s effect!

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:03.740
The real fight is only getting started!

00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:27.380
Dance!  Strike with your heels

00:22:27.640 --> 00:22:30.920
Scream!  You Gotta Go  Raise your voice

00:22:31.340 --> 00:22:34.520
Sing!  Unleash your existence

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:38.560
Get Away!  Until you surpass your limits

00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:42.480
Try It over and over

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:50.640
In this world that spreads forever

00:22:50.990 --> 00:22:57.580
The timeline flows forever

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:00.140
Nothing is certain

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:01.820
In these isolated times

00:23:02.110 --> 00:23:03.550
Set Yourself Free without hesitation

00:23:03.810 --> 00:23:05.320
Cuz We Still Believin' Magic

00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:08.750
The traces we leave behind

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:12.320
The traces we leave behind

00:23:12.520 --> 00:23:16.290
The miracles we create

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:18.500
Never Give Up Never!

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:22.340
I won't give up  Never Give Up Never!

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:40.320
Searching for the truth...  The lost past...

00:23:40.320 --> 00:23:42.860
An irreplaceable friend...

00:23:42.860 --> 00:23:48.300
Ten years have transformed a boy into an envoy of revenge.

00:23:48.300 --> 00:23:53.530
Playmaker musters all his strength to risk everything on his final draw.

00:23:53.530 --> 00:23:57.840
I've done everything I can in order to battle him!

00:23:57.840 --> 00:24:02.490
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
